.env file setup process: 

## Setting Up MongoDB

Option 1: Local MongoDB
1. Download and install MongoDB Community Edition from https://www.mongodb.com/try/download/community
2. Start the MongoDB service:
   - **Windows:** MongoDB runs as a service automatically after install
   - **Mac:** `brew services start mongodb-community`
   - **Linux:** `sudo systemctl start mongod`
3. Add this to your `.env` file:
   `MONGO_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/foresightwallet`


 Option 2: MongoDB Atlas (Cloud — Free)
1. Go to https://www.mongodb.com/cloud/atlas and create a free account
2. Create a new **free cluster** (M0 tier)
3. When prompted, create a **database user** — save the username and password
4. Under Network Access, click **Add IP Address** → select **Allow Access from Anywhere**
5. Go to Database → click **Connect** → choose **Drivers**
6. Copy the connection string — it looks like:
   `mongodb+srv://<username>:<password>@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/`
7. Replace `<username>` and `<password>` with your database user credentials
8. Add this to your `.env` file as:
   `MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://youruser:yourpassword@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/foresightwallet`

## Setting Up Secret Key

Add any random string to your `.env` file as:
`SECRET_KEY=anyrandomstringhere`

For example: `SECRET_KEY=foresightwallet2026`


## Setting Up Gemini API Key

The WalletWise AI chatbot uses Google's Gemini API (gemini-2.5-flash-lite model).

1. Go to https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
2. Sign in with a Google account
3. Click **Create API Key**
4. Copy the key and add it to your `.env` file as:
   `GEMINI_API_KEY=your_key_here`

**Note:** The free tier of Google AI Studio is sufficient to run this project.

## Setting Up Google OAuth 

Google OAuth allows users to sign in with their Google account.

1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/ and sign in
2. Create a new project (or select an existing one)
3. In the left menu go to **APIs & Services** → **OAuth consent screen**
   - Select **External** and click Create
   - Fill in the app name (e.g. Foresight Wallet) and your email
   - Click Save and Continue through the rest of the steps
4. Go to **APIs & Services** → **Credentials**
5. Click **Create Credentials** → **OAuth 2.0 Client ID**
6. Set Application type to **Web application**
7. Under **Authorised redirect URIs** add:
   `http://localhost:5000/google/callback`
8. Click Create — you'll get a **Client ID** and **Client Secret**
9. Add both to your `.env` file:
   `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id_here`
   `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret_here`



## Installation

1. **Clone the repository**
git clone https://github.com/Tahmidislam10/ForesightWallet.git
cd ForesightWallet
2. **Create a virtual environment**
python -m venv venv
3. **Activate the virtual environment**
   - Windows: `venv\Scripts\activate`
   - Mac/Linux: `source venv/bin/activate`
4. **Install dependencies**
pip install -r requirements.txt
5. **Create a `.env` file** in the root folder and add all your keys from the setup sections above:
MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_uri
SECRET_KEY=your_secret_key
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_google_client_id
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your_google_client_secret
6. **Run the application**
python app.py
The application will run locally at:
http://localhost:5000
After this to normallay run application it woild 
venv\Scripts\activate
python app.py
then click on http://127.0.0.1:5000

## Folder Structure

```
ForesightWallet/
├── app.py                          # Flask app factory, registers all blueprints
├── extensions.py                   # MongoDB collections (spending, budget, users)
├── helpers.py                      # Shared utility functions and calculate_month_summary
├── Procfile                        # gunicorn app:app (Render deployment)
├── runtime.txt                     # python-3.10.13
├── requirements.txt                # Python dependencies
├── routes/
│   ├── auth.py                     # Register, login, Google OAuth, logout
│   ├── budget.py                   # Budget tracker + /api/prev-month-balance
│   ├── dashboard.py                # Main dashboard
│   ├── spending.py                 # Spending log CRUD
│   ├── feedback.py                 # Personalised feedback (rule-based)
│   ├── income_trends.py            # Income trends charts
│   ├── spending_trends.py          # Spending trends charts
│   ├── planned_deductions.py       # Planned deductions history
│   ├── prediction.py               # Spending forecast (Random Forest)
│   ├── category_prediction.py      # Top category prediction
│   ├── clustering.py               # K-Means spending behaviour clustering
│   ├── risk.py                     # Financial risk indicator
│   └── walletwise.py               # WalletWise AI chatbot (Gemini API)
├── ml_models/
│   ├── spending_forecast_model.pkl # Random Forest forecast model
│   ├── forecast_feature_cols.pkl   # Feature columns for forecast model
│   ├── kmeans_model.pkl            # K-Means clustering model
│   ├── kmeans_scaler.pkl           # Scaler for K-Means
│   ├── kmeans_feature_cols.pkl     # Feature columns for K-Means
│   └── kmeans_cluster_labels.pkl   # Cluster label mappings
├── static/
│   ├── LogoN.png                   # App logo
│   ├── style.css                   # All styles consolidated
│   └── js/
│       ├── sidebar.js              # Sidebar toggle (desktop + mobile)
│       ├── base.js                 # Dark mode + WalletWise chat
│       ├── budget_tracker.js       # Progress bar, edit toggle, carry forward
│       ├── dashboard.js            # KPI cards, donut charts, bar chart
│       ├── income_trends.js        # Income trends charts
│       ├── planned_deductions.js   # Planned deductions charts
│       ├── prediction.js           # Feature switcher
│       ├── prediction_forecast.js  # Forecast chart
│       ├── spending_log.js         # Spending log interactions
│       └── spending_trends.js      # Spending trends charts
└── templates/
    ├── base.html                   # Sidebar, navbar, dark mode
    ├── dashboard.html              # Main dashboard
    ├── budget_tracker.html         # Budget tracker
    ├── spending_log.html           # Spending log
    ├── income_trends.html          # Income trends
    ├── spending_trends.html        # Spending trends
    ├── planned_deductions.html     # Planned deductions
    ├── prediction.html             # Forecast + category + clustering
    ├── feedback.html               # Personalised feedback
    ├── risk.html                   # Financial risk indicator
    ├── landing.html                # Landing page
    ├── login.html                  # Login page
    └── register.html               # Register page
```




## Tech Stack

| Component | Technology |
|---|---|
| Backend | Python 3.10, Flask 3.0.2 |
| Templating | Jinja2 |
| Database | MongoDB (PyMongo 4.16.0) |
| Frontend | HTML, CSS, JavaScript, Bootstrap 5.3.2 |
| Charts | ApexCharts 3.44.0 |
| ML Models | scikit-learn 1.8.0, joblib 1.3.2 |
| AI Chatbot | Google Gemini API (gemini-2.5-flash-lite) |
| Authentication | Google OAuth 2.0, Flask-Bcrypt |
| Deployment | Render (gunicorn 21.2.0) |
| PDF Export | jsPDF, html2canvas |


